Overlap in x: `ball.x + r > brick.x` and `ball.x - r < brick.x + brick.w`. The penetration depth on x = min((ball.x + r) - brick.x, (brick.x + brick.w) - (ball.x - r)). Actually the penetration is the minimum distance to push out. If ball's right edge is beyond left edge, distance to push left is `(ball.x+r) - brick.x`. If ball's left edge beyond right edge, push right distance is `(brick.x+w) - (ball.x-r)`. The smaller is the push direction.

